{
  "info": {
    "name": "Discord DMs & Moderation",
    "description": "Discord DMs and Moderation through the Gateway, run top to bottom as one shift: a moderator and a junior mod register, a team opens a shift, the junior mod is given records and channels, both negotiate the shift's WebSockets, an applicant is called, the team talks and shares evidence in Discord DMs, and the moderator decides. Ids and tokens are carried from one request to the next automatically.\n\nEverything goes through the Gateway's public port with real tokens: Authorization: Bearer <token>. The Gateway validates it, drops it and tells the service who is calling through X-Player-Id, X-Session-Id, X-Session-Role and X-Record-Access. No request sets those headers to be believed; the last folder checks that the Gateway ignores them.\n\nWebSockets. A client asks the Gateway for an address (POST /ws/negotiate) and then connects to the service directly, so the Gateway is never in the middle of a socket. Folder 1 negotiates Discord DMs' chat socket and Session's live socket, checks that both ports speak only WebSocket (426 to plain HTTP) and that DM checks the token on the handshake itself (401, 403). Newman and the collection runner cannot hold a socket open, so a successful handshake is left to the live demo below. Moderation has no socket of its own: its decisions reach the players through Session's live socket, as score_updated.\n\nLive demo in the Postman app:\n1. Run folders 0 and 1, then copy the collection variables dmSocketUrl and sessionSocketUrl (current values).\n2. New > WebSocket, paste sessionSocketUrl, Connect. Open a second WebSocket tab with dmSocketUrl and send {\"type\":\"join\",\"channelId\":\"<generalChannelId>\"}: a presence frame comes back.\n3. Run folders 2 and 3: Session's socket shows shift_started and applicant_changed; DM's socket shows each message and shared document as it is posted. Sending {\"type\":\"message\",\"channelId\":\"<generalChannelId>\",\"content\":\"hi\"} on the socket posts too.\n4. Run folder 4: \"Moderator decides\" makes Session's socket push score_updated.\nThe two URLs carry a real session token: never save them into an exported collection.\n\nRun it from your machine against the team stack (docker compose up). The defaults match .env.example: the Gateway on http://127.0.0.1:8080, and the WebSocket addresses are whatever the Gateway returns (127.0.0.1:3002 for DM, 3011 for Session). Nothing here uses the internal port 8001, so it does not need to run inside the Docker network:\n\n    npx newman run postman/dm-and-moderation.postman_collection.json\n\nUniversity Record does not yet learn of new applicants, so the junior mod shares the academic year, a record every session can read, rather than the applicant's enrollment.",
    "schema": "https://schema.getpostman.com/json/collection/v2.1.0/collection.json"
  },
  "variable": [{"key": "gatewayBaseUrl", "value": "http://127.0.0.1:8080"}],
  "item": [
    {
      "name": "0. Setup: players, a team and a shift",
      "item": [
        {
          "name": "Register moderator",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "prerequest",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "// A fresh username each run, so re-running never hits 409.",
                  "pm.collectionVariables.set('moderatorName', 'moderator' + Date.now());"
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('201', () => pm.response.to.have.status(201));",
                  "const v = pm.collectionVariables;",
                  "v.set('moderatorId', pm.response.json().playerId);",
                  "v.set('moderatorToken', pm.response.json().token);"
                ]
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [{"key": "Content-Type", "value": "application/json"}],
            "url": "{{gatewayBaseUrl}}/player/auth/register",
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"username\": \"{{moderatorName}}\",\n  \"email\": \"{{moderatorName}}@utm.md\",\n  \"password\": \"correcthorse1\"\n}"
            }
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "Register junior mod",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "prerequest",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": ["pm.collectionVariables.set('juniorName', 'juniormod' + Date.now());"]
              }
            },
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('201', () => pm.response.to.have.status(201));",
                  "const v = pm.collectionVariables;",
                  "v.set('juniorId', pm.response.json().playerId);",
                  "v.set('juniorToken', pm.response.json().token);"
                ]
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [{"key": "Content-Type", "value": "application/json"}],
            "url": "{{gatewayBaseUrl}}/player/auth/register",
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"username\": \"{{juniorName}}\",\n  \"email\": \"{{juniorName}}@utm.md\",\n  \"password\": \"correcthorse1\"\n}"
            }
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "Create team",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('201', () => pm.response.to.have.status(201));",
                  "pm.collectionVariables.set('teamId', pm.response.json().teamId);"
                ]
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              {"key": "Authorization", "value": "Bearer {{moderatorToken}}"},
              {"key": "Content-Type", "value": "application/json"}
            ],
            "url": "{{gatewayBaseUrl}}/player/teams",
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"name\": \"FCIM Night Shift\",\n  \"ownerId\": \"{{moderatorId}}\"\n}"
            }
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "Add the junior mod to the team",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {"type": "text/javascript", "exec": ["pm.test('201', () => pm.response.to.have.status(201));"]}
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              {"key": "Authorization", "value": "Bearer {{moderatorToken}}"},
              {"key": "Content-Type", "value": "application/json"}
            ],
            "url": "{{gatewayBaseUrl}}/player/teams/{{teamId}}/members",
            "body": {"mode": "raw", "raw": "{\n  \"playerId\": \"{{juniorId}}\"\n}"}
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "Open a shift for the team",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('201', () => pm.response.to.have.status(201));",
                  "const v = pm.collectionVariables;",
                  "const body = pm.response.json();",
                  "v.set('sessionId', body.sessionId);",
                  "v.set('moderatorSessionToken', body.sessionToken);"
                ]
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [{"key": "Authorization", "value": "Bearer {{moderatorToken}}"}],
            "url": "{{gatewayBaseUrl}}/player/teams/{{teamId}}/sessions"
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "Junior mod joins",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('200', () => pm.response.to.have.status(200));",
                  "pm.collectionVariables.set('juniorSessionToken', pm.response.json().sessionToken);"
                ]
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [{"key": "Authorization", "value": "Bearer {{juniorToken}}"}],
            "url": "{{gatewayBaseUrl}}/session/sessions/{{sessionId}}/join"
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "Assign the junior mod records and channels",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {"type": "text/javascript", "exec": ["pm.test('200', () => pm.response.to.have.status(200));"]}
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              {"key": "Authorization", "value": "Bearer {{moderatorSessionToken}}"},
              {"key": "Content-Type", "value": "application/json"}
            ],
            "url": "{{gatewayBaseUrl}}/session/sessions/{{sessionId}}/roles",
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"assignments\": [\n    {\n      \"playerId\": \"{{juniorId}}\",\n      \"role\": \"junior_mod\",\n      \"recordAccess\": [\n        \"enrollment\"\n      ],\n      \"channelAccess\": [\n        \"enrollment-check\",\n        \"general-mod-chat\"\n      ]\n    }\n  ]\n}"
            }
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "1. WebSockets: negotiation and handshake",
      "item": [
        {
          "name": "Negotiate the Discord DMs socket",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('200', () => pm.response.to.have.status(200));",
                  "const v = pm.collectionVariables;",
                  "const url = pm.response.json().url;",
                  "pm.test('the Gateway hands out DM\\'s own socket, not its own address', () => {",
                  "  pm.expect(url).to.match(/^wss?:\\/\\//);",
                  "  pm.expect(url).to.include('/ws?sessionId=' + v.get('sessionId'));",
                  "});",
                  "pm.test('no token in the negotiated address', () => pm.expect(url).to.not.include('token='));",
                  "// For a live demo: paste dmSocketUrl into a Postman WebSocket request.",
                  "v.set('dmSocketUrl', url + '&token=' + v.get('moderatorSessionToken'));",
                  "v.set('dmSocketHttpBase', url.replace(/^ws/, 'http').match(/^https?:\\/\\/[^/]+/)[0]);"
                ]
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              {"key": "Authorization", "value": "Bearer {{moderatorSessionToken}}"},
              {"key": "Content-Type", "value": "application/json"}
            ],
            "url": "{{gatewayBaseUrl}}/ws/negotiate",
            "body": {"mode": "raw", "raw": "{\n  \"surface\": \"dm\",\n  \"sessionId\": \"{{sessionId}}\"\n}"}
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "Negotiate Session's live socket",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('200', () => pm.response.to.have.status(200));",
                  "const v = pm.collectionVariables;",
                  "const url = pm.response.json().url;",
                  "pm.test('Session\\'s live socket for this shift', () => pm.expect(url).to.include('/sessions/' + v.get('sessionId') + '/live'));",
                  "// Moderation's decisions show up here as score_updated.",
                  "v.set('sessionSocketUrl', url + '?token=' + v.get('moderatorSessionToken'));",
                  "v.set('sessionSocketHttpBase', url.replace(/^ws/, 'http').match(/^https?:\\/\\/[^/]+/)[0]);"
                ]
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              {"key": "Authorization", "value": "Bearer {{moderatorSessionToken}}"},
              {"key": "Content-Type", "value": "application/json"}
            ],
            "url": "{{gatewayBaseUrl}}/ws/negotiate",
            "body": {"mode": "raw", "raw": "{\n  \"surface\": \"session\",\n  \"sessionId\": \"{{sessionId}}\"\n}"}
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "Negotiation needs a session token, not a player token",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('401', () => pm.response.to.have.status(401));",
                  "pm.test('error is INVALID_TOKEN', () => pm.expect(pm.response.json().error).to.eql('INVALID_TOKEN'));"
                ]
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              {"key": "Authorization", "value": "Bearer {{moderatorToken}}"},
              {"key": "Content-Type", "value": "application/json"}
            ],
            "url": "{{gatewayBaseUrl}}/ws/negotiate",
            "body": {"mode": "raw", "raw": "{\n  \"surface\": \"dm\",\n  \"sessionId\": \"{{sessionId}}\"\n}"}
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "Negotiation for another session is refused",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('403', () => pm.response.to.have.status(403));",
                  "pm.test('error is SESSION_MISMATCH', () => pm.expect(pm.response.json().error).to.eql('SESSION_MISMATCH'));"
                ]
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              {"key": "Authorization", "value": "Bearer {{moderatorSessionToken}}"},
              {"key": "Content-Type", "value": "application/json"}
            ],
            "url": "{{gatewayBaseUrl}}/ws/negotiate",
            "body": {"mode": "raw", "raw": "{\n  \"surface\": \"dm\",\n  \"sessionId\": \"{{$guid}}\"\n}"}
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "DM's socket port only speaks WebSocket",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('426', () => pm.response.to.have.status(426));",
                  "pm.test('error is UPGRADE_REQUIRED', () => pm.expect(pm.response.json().error).to.eql('UPGRADE_REQUIRED'));",
                  "pm.test('asks for an upgrade to websocket', () => pm.expect(pm.response.headers.get('Upgrade')).to.eql('websocket'));"
                ]
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {"method": "GET", "header": [], "url": "{{dmSocketHttpBase}}/ws?sessionId={{sessionId}}"}
        },
        {
          "name": "DM's socket refuses a handshake with a bad token",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('401', () => pm.response.to.have.status(401));",
                  "pm.test('error is INVALID_TOKEN', () => pm.expect(pm.response.json().error).to.eql('INVALID_TOKEN'));"
                ]
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [
              {"key": "Connection", "value": "Upgrade"},
              {"key": "Upgrade", "value": "websocket"},
              {"key": "Sec-WebSocket-Version", "value": "13"},
              {"key": "Sec-WebSocket-Key", "value": "dGhlIHNhbXBsZSBub25jZQ=="}
            ],
            "url": "{{dmSocketHttpBase}}/ws?sessionId={{sessionId}}&token=not-a-token"
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "DM's socket refuses a token from another session",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('403', () => pm.response.to.have.status(403));",
                  "pm.test('error is SESSION_MISMATCH', () => pm.expect(pm.response.json().error).to.eql('SESSION_MISMATCH'));"
                ]
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [
              {"key": "Connection", "value": "Upgrade"},
              {"key": "Upgrade", "value": "websocket"},
              {"key": "Sec-WebSocket-Version", "value": "13"},
              {"key": "Sec-WebSocket-Key", "value": "dGhlIHNhbXBsZSBub25jZQ=="}
            ],
            "url": "{{dmSocketHttpBase}}/ws?sessionId={{$guid}}&token={{moderatorSessionToken}}"
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "Session's socket port only speaks WebSocket",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {"type": "text/javascript", "exec": ["pm.test('426', () => pm.response.to.have.status(426));"]}
            }
          ],
          "request": {"method": "GET", "header": [], "url": "{{sessionSocketHttpBase}}/sessions/{{sessionId}}/live"}
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "2. The shift starts",
      "item": [
        {
          "name": "Start the shift",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('200', () => pm.response.to.have.status(200));",
                  "pm.test('active', () => pm.expect(pm.response.json().status).to.eql('active'));"
                ]
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [{"key": "Authorization", "value": "Bearer {{moderatorSessionToken}}"}],
            "url": "{{gatewayBaseUrl}}/session/sessions/{{sessionId}}/start"
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "Junior mod picks up its record access",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('200', () => pm.response.to.have.status(200));",
                  "pm.collectionVariables.set('juniorSessionToken', pm.response.json().sessionToken);"
                ]
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [{"key": "Authorization", "value": "Bearer {{juniorToken}}"}],
            "url": "{{gatewayBaseUrl}}/session/sessions/{{sessionId}}/token"
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "Call the next applicant",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('202', () => pm.response.to.have.status(202));",
                  "pm.collectionVariables.set('applicantId', pm.response.json().applicantId);"
                ]
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [{"key": "Authorization", "value": "Bearer {{moderatorSessionToken}}"}],
            "url": "{{gatewayBaseUrl}}/session/sessions/{{sessionId}}/next-applicant"
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "3. Discord DMs",
      "item": [
        {
          "name": "List channels (moderator)",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('200', () => pm.response.to.have.status(200));",
                  "const v = pm.collectionVariables;",
                  "const byName = Object.fromEntries(pm.response.json().map((c) => [c.name, c.channelId]));",
                  "pm.test('the four default channels', () => pm.expect(Object.keys(byName)).to.have.members(['enrollment-check', 'faculty-check', 'course-registration', 'general-mod-chat']));",
                  "v.set('generalChannelId', byName['general-mod-chat']);",
                  "v.set('facultyChannelId', byName['faculty-check']);"
                ]
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [{"key": "Authorization", "value": "Bearer {{moderatorSessionToken}}"}],
            "url": "{{gatewayBaseUrl}}/dm/sessions/{{sessionId}}/channels"
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "List channels (junior mod, only the assigned ones)",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('200', () => pm.response.to.have.status(200));",
                  "pm.test('Session\\'s access-check decides', () => pm.expect(pm.response.json().map((c) => c.name)).to.have.members(['enrollment-check', 'general-mod-chat']));"
                ]
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [{"key": "Authorization", "value": "Bearer {{juniorSessionToken}}"}],
            "url": "{{gatewayBaseUrl}}/dm/sessions/{{sessionId}}/channels"
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "Create a channel",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {"type": "text/javascript", "exec": ["pm.test('201', () => pm.response.to.have.status(201));"]}
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              {"key": "Authorization", "value": "Bearer {{moderatorSessionToken}}"},
              {"key": "Content-Type", "value": "application/json"}
            ],
            "url": "{{gatewayBaseUrl}}/dm/sessions/{{sessionId}}/channels",
            "body": {"mode": "raw", "raw": "{\n  \"names\": [\n    \"evidence\"\n  ]\n}"}
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "Junior mod cannot create channels",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('403', () => pm.response.to.have.status(403));",
                  "pm.test('error is ROLE_NOT_ALLOWED', () => pm.expect(pm.response.json().error).to.eql('ROLE_NOT_ALLOWED'));"
                ]
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              {"key": "Authorization", "value": "Bearer {{juniorSessionToken}}"},
              {"key": "Content-Type", "value": "application/json"}
            ],
            "url": "{{gatewayBaseUrl}}/dm/sessions/{{sessionId}}/channels",
            "body": {"mode": "raw", "raw": "{\n  \"names\": [\n    \"side-chat\"\n  ]\n}"}
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "Post a message",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('201', () => pm.response.to.have.status(201));",
                  "pm.test('the author is the token\\'s player', () => pm.expect(pm.response.json().authorId).to.eql(pm.collectionVariables.get('moderatorId')));"
                ]
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              {"key": "Authorization", "value": "Bearer {{moderatorSessionToken}}"},
              {"key": "Content-Type", "value": "application/json"}
            ],
            "url": "{{gatewayBaseUrl}}/dm/channels/{{generalChannelId}}/messages",
            "body": {"mode": "raw", "raw": "{\n  \"content\": \"Checking the student ID now.\"\n}"}
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "Junior mod cannot post to an unassigned channel",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('403', () => pm.response.to.have.status(403));",
                  "pm.test('error is CHANNEL_ACCESS_DENIED', () => pm.expect(pm.response.json().error).to.eql('CHANNEL_ACCESS_DENIED'));"
                ]
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              {"key": "Authorization", "value": "Bearer {{juniorSessionToken}}"},
              {"key": "Content-Type", "value": "application/json"}
            ],
            "url": "{{gatewayBaseUrl}}/dm/channels/{{facultyChannelId}}/messages",
            "body": {"mode": "raw", "raw": "{\n  \"content\": \"let me in\"\n}"}
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "Read the applicant's documents (Credential)",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('200', () => pm.response.to.have.status(200));",
                  "pm.collectionVariables.set('credentialId', pm.response.json()[0].credentialId);"
                ]
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [{"key": "Authorization", "value": "Bearer {{moderatorSessionToken}}"}],
            "url": "{{gatewayBaseUrl}}/credential/applicants/{{applicantId}}/credentials"
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "Moderator shares a document",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('201', () => pm.response.to.have.status(201));",
                  "pm.test('posted as an attachment from Credential', () => pm.expect(pm.response.json().attachment.source).to.eql('credential'));"
                ]
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              {"key": "Authorization", "value": "Bearer {{moderatorSessionToken}}"},
              {"key": "Content-Type", "value": "application/json"}
            ],
            "url": "{{gatewayBaseUrl}}/dm/channels/{{generalChannelId}}/messages",
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"share\": {\n    \"applicantId\": \"{{applicantId}}\",\n    \"source\": \"credential\",\n    \"credentialId\": \"{{credentialId}}\"\n  }\n}"
            }
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "Junior mod cannot share a document",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('403', () => pm.response.to.have.status(403));",
                  "pm.test('error is SHARE_DENIED', () => pm.expect(pm.response.json().error).to.eql('SHARE_DENIED'));"
                ]
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              {"key": "Authorization", "value": "Bearer {{juniorSessionToken}}"},
              {"key": "Content-Type", "value": "application/json"}
            ],
            "url": "{{gatewayBaseUrl}}/dm/channels/{{generalChannelId}}/messages",
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"share\": {\n    \"applicantId\": \"{{applicantId}}\",\n    \"source\": \"credential\",\n    \"credentialId\": \"{{credentialId}}\"\n  }\n}"
            }
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "Junior mod shares the academic year (University Record)",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('201', () => pm.response.to.have.status(201));",
                  "pm.test('posted as an attachment from University Record', () => pm.expect(pm.response.json().attachment.source).to.eql('academic-year'));"
                ]
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              {"key": "Authorization", "value": "Bearer {{juniorSessionToken}}"},
              {"key": "Content-Type", "value": "application/json"}
            ],
            "url": "{{gatewayBaseUrl}}/dm/channels/{{generalChannelId}}/messages",
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"share\": {\n    \"applicantId\": \"{{applicantId}}\",\n    \"source\": \"academic-year\"\n  }\n}"
            }
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "Read the channel history",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('200', () => pm.response.to.have.status(200));",
                  "const sources = pm.response.json().map((m) => m.attachment ? m.attachment.source : 'text');",
                  "pm.test('newest first: academic year, document, text', () => pm.expect(sources).to.eql(['academic-year', 'credential', 'text']));"
                ]
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [{"key": "Authorization", "value": "Bearer {{juniorSessionToken}}"}],
            "url": "{{gatewayBaseUrl}}/dm/channels/{{generalChannelId}}/messages?limit=10"
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "4. Moderation",
      "item": [
        {
          "name": "Junior mod cannot decide",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('403', () => pm.response.to.have.status(403));",
                  "pm.test('error is ROLE_NOT_ALLOWED', () => pm.expect(pm.response.json().error).to.eql('ROLE_NOT_ALLOWED'));"
                ]
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              {"key": "Authorization", "value": "Bearer {{juniorSessionToken}}"},
              {"key": "Content-Type", "value": "application/json"}
            ],
            "url": "{{gatewayBaseUrl}}/moderation/decisions",
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"sessionId\": \"{{sessionId}}\",\n  \"applicantId\": \"{{applicantId}}\",\n  \"action\": \"accept\"\n}"
            }
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "Moderator decides",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('201', () => pm.response.to.have.status(201));",
                  "const d = pm.response.json();",
                  "pm.collectionVariables.set('decisionId', d.decisionId);",
                  "pm.collectionVariables.set('decisionPenalty', d.penalty);",
                  "pm.collectionVariables.set('decisionCorrect', d.correct);",
                  "pm.test('the moderator is the token\\'s player', () => pm.expect(d.moderatorId).to.eql(pm.collectionVariables.get('moderatorId')));",
                  "pm.test('judged: correct matches outcome', () => pm.expect(d.correct).to.eql(d.outcome === 'correct'));",
                  "pm.test('penalty matches outcome', () => pm.expect(d.penalty).to.eql({ correct: 0, wrong_reject: 10, wrong_admit: 20, missed_ban: 30 }[d.outcome]));"
                ]
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              {"key": "Authorization", "value": "Bearer {{moderatorSessionToken}}"},
              {"key": "Content-Type", "value": "application/json"}
            ],
            "url": "{{gatewayBaseUrl}}/moderation/decisions",
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"sessionId\": \"{{sessionId}}\",\n  \"applicantId\": \"{{applicantId}}\",\n  \"action\": \"accept\"\n}"
            }
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "The same applicant cannot be decided twice",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('409', () => pm.response.to.have.status(409));",
                  "pm.test('error is DECISION_EXISTS', () => pm.expect(pm.response.json().error).to.eql('DECISION_EXISTS'));"
                ]
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              {"key": "Authorization", "value": "Bearer {{moderatorSessionToken}}"},
              {"key": "Content-Type", "value": "application/json"}
            ],
            "url": "{{gatewayBaseUrl}}/moderation/decisions",
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"sessionId\": \"{{sessionId}}\",\n  \"applicantId\": \"{{applicantId}}\",\n  \"action\": \"ban\"\n}"
            }
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "Read the decision",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {"type": "text/javascript", "exec": ["pm.test('200', () => pm.response.to.have.status(200));"]}
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [{"key": "Authorization", "value": "Bearer {{juniorSessionToken}}"}],
            "url": "{{gatewayBaseUrl}}/moderation/decisions/{{decisionId}}"
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "The shift's decision log",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('200', () => pm.response.to.have.status(200));",
                  "pm.test('holds the decision', () => pm.expect(pm.response.json().map((d) => d.decisionId)).to.eql([pm.collectionVariables.get('decisionId')]));"
                ]
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [{"key": "Authorization", "value": "Bearer {{moderatorSessionToken}}"}],
            "url": "{{gatewayBaseUrl}}/moderation/sessions/{{sessionId}}/decisions"
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "Session counted the decision",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('200', () => pm.response.to.have.status(200));",
                  "const v = pm.collectionVariables;",
                  "const s = pm.response.json();",
                  "const expected = (v.get('decisionCorrect') === true || v.get('decisionCorrect') === 'true' ? 10 : 0) - Number(v.get('decisionPenalty'));",
                  "pm.test('one application processed', () => pm.expect(s.applicationsProcessed).to.eql(1));",
                  "pm.test('score follows the decision (also pushed live as score_updated)', () => pm.expect(s.score).to.eql(expected));"
                ]
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [{"key": "Authorization", "value": "Bearer {{moderatorSessionToken}}"}],
            "url": "{{gatewayBaseUrl}}/session/sessions/{{sessionId}}"
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "5. The Gateway boundary",
      "item": [
        {
          "name": "No token is refused by the Gateway",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('401', () => pm.response.to.have.status(401));",
                  "pm.test('error is INVALID_TOKEN', () => pm.expect(pm.response.json().error).to.eql('INVALID_TOKEN'));"
                ]
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {"method": "GET", "header": [], "url": "{{gatewayBaseUrl}}/dm/sessions/{{sessionId}}/channels"}
        },
        {
          "name": "Identity headers without a token are not believed",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('401', () => pm.response.to.have.status(401));",
                  "pm.test('error is INVALID_TOKEN', () => pm.expect(pm.response.json().error).to.eql('INVALID_TOKEN'));"
                ]
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [
              {"key": "X-Player-Id", "value": "{{moderatorId}}"},
              {"key": "X-Session-Id", "value": "{{sessionId}}"},
              {"key": "X-Session-Role", "value": "moderator"}
            ],
            "url": "{{gatewayBaseUrl}}/dm/sessions/{{sessionId}}/channels"
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "The token decides the role, not a header",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('403', () => pm.response.to.have.status(403));",
                  "pm.test('error is ROLE_NOT_ALLOWED', () => pm.expect(pm.response.json().error).to.eql('ROLE_NOT_ALLOWED'));"
                ]
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              {"key": "Authorization", "value": "Bearer {{juniorSessionToken}}"},
              {"key": "X-Session-Role", "value": "moderator"},
              {"key": "Content-Type", "value": "application/json"}
            ],
            "url": "{{gatewayBaseUrl}}/dm/sessions/{{sessionId}}/channels",
            "body": {"mode": "raw", "raw": "{\n  \"names\": [\n    \"not-allowed\"\n  ]\n}"}
          }
        }
      ]
    }
  ]
}
